rbi_user_data_state.riskMatrix:
{
  "cof_labels": ["1", "2", "3", "4", "5"],
  "pof_labels": ["5", "4", "3", "2", "1"],
  "description": "5×5 matrix: CoF ranks A–E across the top; M6 labels columns A, low … E, high. PoF row labels 5 high → 1 low (5 = highest frequency … 1 = lowest). M6 shows cells as PoF + letter (e.g. 3C for key 33). Cell keys stay two-digit rank order (e.g. 33 = CoF rank 3, PoF 3). Legacy CoF-letter keys (e.g. C3) still work in cells. These colors are used for the matrix in M6."
}

